<title>BELGIUM: EU farm ministers to be pressed on transport rules.</title>
<headline>EU farm ministers to be pressed on transport rules.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers will be pressed to agree new legislation on the transport of live animals when they meet in Luxembourg next week.</p>
<p>&quot;The United Kingdom will be asking for urgent action on two pieces of legislation on staging posts and on livestock vehicles which were due to be agreed in July,&quot; a British official said.</p>
<p>A directive on the transport of animals has been agreed but it requires two further pieces of legislation to be effective, the official explained.</p>
</text>
